\section{Finite-Step Regional Capture of the Live MEKF}
\label{sec:finite-live-capture}

The startup certificate is formulated on the compact handoff set actually
produced by the source.  It need not first be embedded in a common outer radius.
The complete nonlinear Live map is propagated as a set until it reaches a
robustly invariant inner region; bounded transient growth is permitted provided
every prefix remains in the declared proof-safe domain.

\subsection{Exact lifted map and safe domain}

Let $\pi_k$ contain the complete source proof mode at sample $k$: covariance,
accelerometer-bias enable state, magnetic-gauge state, staged OU/$R_S$
parameters, pseudo-update phase, and accepted-update pattern.  Only sequences in
the source-reachable family $\Pi^{\rm src}_{k,m}$ of
Sec.~\ref{sec:iss-source-family} are admissible.  For a lift of $m\ge1$ samples,
write the exact implemented error map as
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \vct e_{k+m}=\mathcal F_{k,m}
 (\vct e_k,\vct d_{k:k+m-1};\pi_{k:k+m}).}
 \label{eq:capture-exact-lift}
\end{equation}
It contains exact prediction, every accepted accelerometer and magnetometer
correction, the full $S=0$ Kalman correction and its cross-covariance gain,
quaternion injection/reset, covariance propagation, source enable-state
transitions, and the predictable parameter schedule.

Let $\mathcal D_k$ be a compact chart-, covariance-, measurement-, and
source-mode-safe domain on which the complete map is continuous.  Let
$\mathcal B_k\Subset\mathcal D_k$ be a compact inner regional set.  The proof
does not require the handoff family to be a ball, ellipsoid, or Cartesian
product.

For a compact $X\subset\mathcal D_k$ and deterministic mismatch budget
$\|\vct d\|_\infty\le\bar d$, define the exact reachable-set operator
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathfrak T_{k,m}(X;\bar d):=
 \left\{
 \mathcal F_{k,m}(\vct e,\vct d;\pi):
 \begin{array}{l}
 \vct e\in X,\ \|\vct d\|_\infty\le\bar d,\\
 \pi\in\Pi^{\rm src}_{k,m}
 \end{array}
 \right\}.}
 \label{eq:capture-set-envelope}
\end{equation}
For $1\le j<m$, $\mathfrak T^{\rm pre}_{k,j}$ is defined by the corresponding
prefix map.  Continuity on compact families makes these sets compact.  The
operator is inclusion-monotone:
\begin{equation}
 X\subseteq Y
 \quad\Longrightarrow\quad
 \mathfrak T_{k,m}(X;\bar d)
 \subseteq\mathfrak T_{k,m}(Y;\bar d).
 \label{eq:capture-comparison-monotone}
\end{equation}

Choose source-admissible lift lengths $m_n\ge1$, set $k_0=k_H$ and
$k_{n+1}=k_n+m_n$, and propagate
\begin{equation}
 X_0=\mathcal H_{k_H},
 \qquad
 X_{n+1}=\mathfrak T_{k_n,m_n}(X_n;\bar d).
 \label{eq:capture-comparison-sequence}
\end{equation}
Here $\mathcal H_{k_H}$ is the structured handoff family supplied by the startup
analysis.  Different lifts may use different source-reachable schedules and
accepted-update patterns.

\subsection{Direct handoff-to-inner-set capture}

Let $V_k:\mathcal D_k\rightarrow\mathbb R_+$ be continuous and uniformly
positive definite with respect to the chosen gauge-referenced error metric on
$\mathcal B_k$.  Assume that every admissible post-capture lift has safe
prefixes and satisfies, for some $0<\lambda_B<1$ and class-$\mathcal K$
function $\gamma_B$,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 V_{k+m}(\mathcal F_{k,m}(\vct e,\vct d;\pi))
 \le \lambda_B V_k(\vct e)+\gamma_B(\bar d),
 \qquad \vct e\in\mathcal B_k.}
 \label{eq:capture-inner-contraction}
\end{equation}
The disturbance budget is chosen so that the right-hand side remains inside the
sublevel defining $\mathcal B_{k+m}$; equivalently,
\begin{equation}
 \mathfrak T_{k,m}(\mathcal B_k;\bar d)
 \subseteq\mathcal B_{k+m}.
 \label{eq:capture-inner-invariance}
\end{equation}

\begin{theorem}[Source-shaped finite Live capture and practical ISS]
\label{thm:finite-live-capture}
Suppose the handoff sequence of Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-comparison-sequence}
has a finite $N_H$ such that
\begin{align}
 X_n&\subseteq\mathcal D_{k_n},
 &&0\le n\le N_H,
 \label{eq:capture-lift-domain}\\
 \mathfrak T^{\rm pre}_{k_n,j}(X_n;\bar d)
 &\subseteq\mathcal D_{k_n+j},
 &&0\le n<N_H,\quad1\le j<m_n,
 \label{eq:capture-prefix-domain}\\
 X_{N_H}&\subseteq\mathcal B_{k_{N_H}}.
 \label{eq:capture-finite-entry}
\end{align}
If Eqs.~\eqref{eq:capture-inner-contraction}--
\eqref{eq:capture-inner-invariance} hold thereafter, every deterministic Live
trajectory starting in $\mathcal H_{k_H}$ remains in the proof-safe domain,
enters the inner regional set after at most $N_H$ lifted intervals, and remains
there.  At post-capture lifted index $j$,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 V_{k_{N_H+j}}
 \le \lambda_B^j V_{k_{N_H}}
 +\frac{1-\lambda_B^j}{1-\lambda_B}\gamma_B(\bar d).}
 \label{eq:capture-practical-iss}
\end{equation}
For $\bar d=0$, the captured error converges exponentially to the adopted gauge
within the inner regional domain.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Equation~\eqref{eq:capture-set-envelope} contains every admissible image of
$X_n$.  Induction with Eqs.~\eqref{eq:capture-lift-domain}--
\eqref{eq:capture-prefix-domain} therefore keeps the complete sample-by-sample
trajectory in $\mathcal D$.  Equation~\eqref{eq:capture-finite-entry} gives
finite entry into $\mathcal B$.  Forward invariance follows from
Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-inner-invariance}, and iteration of
Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-inner-contraction} gives the geometric bound.
\end{proof}

The startup time bound follows directly from the source-specific sequence:
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 N_H:=\min\{n:X_n\subseteq\mathcal B_{k_n}\},
 \qquad
 T_H\le h_+\sum_{n=0}^{N_H-1}m_n.}
 \label{eq:capture-count}
\end{equation}
No inclusion of $\mathcal H$ in a separate generic outer capture set is needed.

\subsection{Structured computational enclosures}

For numerical enclosure it is useful to report dimensionless block radii without
making them the theorem's state space.  Choose uniformly positive-definite
metrics and define
\begin{align}
 r_{\xi,k}(\vct e)
 &=\bigl(\vct e_\xi^\top\mat Q_\xi(\pi_k)\vct e_\xi\bigr)^{1/2},\\
 r_{\ell,k}(\vct e)
 &=\bigl(\vct e_\ell^\top\mat Q_\ell(\pi_k)\vct e_\ell\bigr)^{1/2},\\
 \vct r_k(\vct e)&=(r_{\xi,k},r_{\ell,k})^\top,
 \label{eq:capture-structured-radii}
\end{align}
with $\vct e_\ell=(\delta\vct v,\delta\vct p)$ and the remaining active
coordinates in $\vct e_\xi$.  The corresponding enclosure is
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal C_k(\vct a)
 :=\{\vct e:\vct r_k(\vct e)\preceq\vct a\}.
 \label{eq:capture-structured-box}
\end{equation}
For a compact set $X$, define its radius enclosure
\begin{equation}
 \mathcal R_k(X):=
 \begin{bmatrix}
 \sup_{e\in X}r_{\xi,k}(e)\\
 \sup_{e\in X}r_{\ell,k}(e)
 \end{bmatrix}.
 \label{eq:capture-radius-enclosure}
\end{equation}
Then $X\subseteq\mathcal C_k(\mathcal R_k(X))$.  The two suprema need not be
attained by the same physical state, so propagation of $X$ itself is the
certificate object; $\mathcal C_k(\mathcal R_k(X))$ is an optional outer
approximation used by a verifier when convenient.

A radius-only implementation may define
\begin{equation}
 [\mathcal T_{k,m}(\vct a;\bar d)]_i
 :=\sup\{r_{i,k+m}(e^+):
 e\in\mathcal C_k(\vct a),\ e^+\in
 \mathfrak T_{k,m}(\{e\};\bar d)\},
 \quad i\in\{\xi,\ell\},
 \label{eq:capture-comparison-envelope}
\end{equation}
but this is sufficient rather than necessary for
Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-live-capture}.

\subsection{Operational certificate contract}
\label{sec:capture-certificate-contract}

The verifier starts at the exact covariance and source mode produced by
\texttt{goLive()}, including the enabled linear block, staged OU parameters,
full $S=0$ gain, pseudo-update phase, and the accelerometer-bias hold.  The
certificate reports at least
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \{\mathcal H,\mathcal D,\mathcal B,
 N_H,T_H,B_{\rm pre},\lambda_B,\gamma_B\},}
 \label{eq:capture-certificate-outputs}
\end{equation}
where $B_{\rm pre}$ is the largest verified normalized prefix amplification.
If radius enclosures are used, the corresponding
$\mathcal R_k(\mathcal H)$, $\mathcal R_k(\mathcal D)$ and
$\mathcal R_k(\mathcal B)$ are reported as diagnostic summaries.
The deterministic pass conditions are
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathcal H_{k_H}\subseteq\mathcal D_{k_H},
 \qquad N_H<\infty,
 \qquad X_{N_H}\subseteq\mathcal B_{k_{N_H}},
 \qquad \lambda_B<1,}
 \label{eq:capture-certificate-pass}
\end{equation}
together with the prefix-safety and inner-invariance conditions.

\subsection{Stochastic Live qualification}
\label{sec:capture-stochastic}

Gaussian process and measurement noise are not represented by a deterministic
infinite-horizon supremum.  Let $\mathscr F_n$ be the filtration at captured
lifted indices and let $V_n$ be the same nonnegative regional Lyapunov measure.

\begin{theorem}[Mean-square practical stability under stochastic Live noise]
\label{thm:capture-stochastic-live}
Assume the exact stochastic lifted map remains in the certified stochastic
regional domain and satisfies the conditional drift inequality
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathbb E[V_{n+1}\mid\mathscr F_n]
 \le\lambda_s V_n+\sigma_s^2,
 \qquad 0<\lambda_s<1.}
 \label{eq:capture-stochastic-drift}
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \mathbb E V_n
 \le\lambda_s^n\mathbb E V_0
 +\frac{1-\lambda_s^n}{1-\lambda_s}\sigma_s^2.}
 \label{eq:capture-stochastic-ms}
\end{equation}
Moreover, for any $a>0$ and finite horizon $N$,
\begin{equation}
 \boxed{
 \Pr\!\left(\max_{0\le n\le N}V_n\ge a\right)
 \le \frac{1}{a}
 \sum_{n=0}^{N}\left(
 \lambda_s^n\mathbb E V_0+
 \frac{\sigma_s^2}{1-\lambda_s}\right).}
 \label{eq:capture-stochastic-finite-hp}
\end{equation}
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Taking expectations in Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-stochastic-drift} and iterating
gives Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-stochastic-ms}.  Markov's inequality followed by a
union bound over the finite horizon gives
Eq.~\eqref{eq:capture-stochastic-finite-hp}.
\end{proof}

Equation~\eqref{eq:capture-stochastic-drift} is a stochastic certificate
condition for the exact implemented map; it is not inferred from the
deterministic bounded-input theorem.
